Pipeline: Orchestrator

Purpose:
  Defines orchestrator pipeline — how user input flows through
  all engines to produce results.

NewProjectPipeline:
  USER INPUT
    ↓
  INTENT NORMALIZATION
    ↓
  PROJECT DISCOVERY
    ↓
  ANALYSIS
    ↓
  ARCHITECTURE
    ↓
  SKILL SELECTION
    ↓
  DECISION
    ↓
  TASK GENERATION
    ↓
  DEPENDENCY GRAPH
    ↓
  WORKFLOW ASSIGNMENT
    ↓
  BDD
    ↓
  IMPLEMENTATION
    ↓
  TEST
    ↓
  SECURITY
    ↓
  PERFORMANCE
    ↓
  INFRASTRUCTURE
    ↓
  RELEASE
    ↓
  DEPLOY
    ↓
  OBSERVE
    ↓
  LEARN

ExistingProjectPipeline:
  USER INPUT
    ↓
  PROJECT SCAN
    ↓
  CODE ANALYSIS
    ↓
  ARCHITECTURE DETECTION
    ↓
  DOMAIN DETECTION
    ↓
  DEPENDENCY DETECTION
    ↓
  SECURITY DETECTION
    ↓
  INFRASTRUCTURE DETECTION
    ↓
  DOCUMENTATION DETECTION
    ↓
  .sdd MAPPING
    ↓
  CONFLICT REPORT
    ↓
  BASELINE
    ↓
  SKILL GAP ANALYSIS
    ↓
  SKILL RECOMMENDATION
    ↓
  TASK GENERATION (from gaps)
    ↓
  WORKFLOW ASSIGNMENT
    ↓
  PARALLEL EXECUTION (where possible)

SkillIntegrationPipeline:
  REQUIREMENT ANALYSIS
    ↓
  SKILL DISCOVERY
    ↓
  RELEVANCE SCORING
    ↓
  GAP ANALYSIS
    ↓
  RECOMMENDATION (>= 80% relevance)
    ↓
  HUMAN APPROVAL
    ↓
  SKILL ACQUISITION
    ↓
  SKILL ADAPTATION
    ↓
  SKILL INTEGRATION
    ↓
  SKILL TESTING
    ↓
  SKILL DEPLOYMENT
    ↓
  KNOWLEDGE SHARING

CrossLayerPipeline:
  API CHANGE
    ↓
  IMPACT ANALYSIS
    ↓
  BE TASK + FE TASK + MD TASK (parallel)
    ↓
  INTEGRATION TEST
    ↓
  DOC TASK
    ↓
  PARALLEL EXECUTION
    ↓
  KNOWLEDGE SHARING
    ↓
  RELEASE

PipelineRules:
  [PL1]  Pipeline is adaptive, not linear.
  [PL2]  Existing project starts with discovery, not architecture.
  [PL3]  Cross-layer changes trigger multi-layer task creation.
  [PL4]  Pipeline MUST support pause/resume for human approval.

State: +
  